      "helpInstruments": "Context: how full this session's context window is; near full, Claude compacts the conversation. 5-hour and 7-day quota: how much of your plan's limits is used. Gauges turn yellow at 60% and red at 80%. Session cost: spend so far, with its trend since you opened this page. Turns: prompts answered. Cache hit: share of the main session's input tokens read from the prompt cache; higher is cheaper. Tokens: sent in and out, subagents included. Click Context to see what fills it. Blocked on you: the time turns waited for your approval. Each tile shows its figure against its limit. Cache hit is green when high. Typical is the median of this project's earlier sessions, marked by a tick. The tick on a quota marks an even pace up to its reset. The pins shake slightly while the page is connected: that movement is decoration, the numbers are exact. Until this project has three earlier sessions, cost and turns compare with a fixed guide, in neutral colour.",
      "helpWaterfall": "Every tool call in the time chosen in the agent flow, in the order it started. A bar shows when the call ran and for how long; a subagent's calls sit under it. Gaps are time the model spent thinking. The slowest call is marked, failures are red and running calls are striped. Click a call for its details.",
      "helpEvents": "What needs you, such as a waiting approval or a failed test. An item that goes away stays here, marked cleared with its time. This browser keeps the history, so a reload keeps it.",
      "helpRunning": "Each tool call running right now, who runs it and for how long.",
      "helpTurns": "One bar per recent turn, showing where its time went: the model, each kind of tool, and waiting for you. The longest turn sets the scale.",
      "helpCalls": "The session's recent tool calls: when, who, what and the result. Click a column head to sort, filter with the box and the buttons, and click a row for its details. An MCP server's tools share one button.",
      "helpInsights": "The calls worth a look: those that took longest, and those whose results were largest in tokens, since large results fill the context. Approvals asked more than once are listed too.",
      "helpVerification": "The last test, lint, typecheck and build command and how each ended. A dash means it has not run yet. A number is how many tests ran, with (−n) skipped. Hover for the whole command. Test files edited are listed below, with the changed lines. The list stays until you press x on its item in the pane. Some updates are right, so check them. A count says how many files changed after the last passing test run.",
      "helpTasks": "Claude's to-do list for this session, and how many items are done.",
      "helpAgents": "One row per subagent: what it does, its type and model, how long it ran, its calls, tokens, cost, errors and files edited. The three dots show its duration, tokens and errors against the session's other subagents: green is fine, amber worth a look, red needs a look. Agents with the worst dots come first, running ones on top; click a column head to sort. More than eight sharing a name before a colon fold into one row. Click a row for the prompt and its calls. Keys: arrows move, Enter opens, Esc closes, f shows the agent's tool calls. FAIL means it reported failing tests; hover for why.",
      "helpFiles": "What this session edited and read, from successful calls. Edited files are grouped by the last test run: after it, they still need a test; before a passing run, they were in place when it passed, which does not prove a test covers them. ×n counts edits or reads; reads count since the last compaction. New marks a watched source file the session created. Hover for the whole path.",
